  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 9.2, 'Critical sustainability elements'. Four interlocking puzzle pieces, each annotated. POLICY: understand the country's policy environment, including gaps in existing policies and strategies. TECHNICAL: map government capacity to manage solutions over the long term, and develop a capacity-building plan for human skills and infrastructure. INSTITUTIONAL: identify the level of engagement and participation across the health system in the design and adaptation of solutions. FINANCIAL: ensure the cost of maintaining and replacing solutions is feasible for the government and built into the right funding mechanism. It appears inside the 'BID Initiative: Sustainability' case study, adapted from the BID Initiative briefs.",
